WEBVTT

00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:06.570
Why don't you stop pretending to be human?

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:12.600
You don't have the right to dream.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.110
You aren't even allowed to laugh.

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:17.600
You're all alone,

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.440
my sister.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:56.260
Forgiveness for the Past

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:02.310
I had her get some rest.

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:04.610
How's Cardia doing?

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:05.930
Dumb question.

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:10.630
After being faced with what 
she really is like that,

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:12.810
of course she'd be confused.

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:18.350
Perhaps that was the objective all along.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:24.280
All of the important documents in the lab 
that had to do with Isaac were stolen.

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:26.990
It was most likely Finis.

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:32.410
He may have known that Cardia 
would go to that lab someday.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:35.100
So he just let all that happen?

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:37.410
Just to hurt Cardia?

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:40.170
I knew.

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:43.670
I always had a feeling

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:47.470
that Cardia was a life form 
created by man...

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:50.880
a homunculus.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:53.750
The Horologium embedded in her chest...

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.430
A body that can withstand its poison...

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:59.150
The daughter of Isaac Beckford...

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:03.440
It wasn't hard to formulate
 the hypothesis from all that.

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:05.260
Why didn't you say anything?

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:06.890
I couldn't.

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:10.540
She's so pure and kind...

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:13.620
She's just a normal girl.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:14.980
Still...

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:19.220
Still, she should have heard it from us.

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:23.390
Rather than someone she trusted 
keeping a cruel secret from her...

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:29.030
She'd have been better off hearing 
the truth and being hurt.

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:31.460
Lupin...

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:40.360
Cardia?

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:41.560
What's wrong?

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:43.520
This beast just took off running.

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:46.810
Hey! You're splattering mud everywhere!

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:47.710
Stop that!

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:48.910
Drac...

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:48.910
Ah, c'mon!

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:51.480
Take care of Sisi, okay?

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:53.910
Take him for walks.

00:03:55.990 --> 00:03:58.160
Sure. You can count on me.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:02.400
You should go to bed, Cardia.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.090
You'll catch a cold.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:04.810
Yeah.

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:12.190
I'm sorry.

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:19.610
Lupin!

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:23.690
You can't go after her! 
You don't know where she went!

00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:26.810
But I can't just sit around and do nothing!

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:28.040
Calm down.

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:32.190
What good will losing your head do?

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:40.220
I can't leave her alone.

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:41.990
Is Cardia...

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.460
all right?

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:57.350
I'm so excited, Mom!

00:04:57.350 --> 00:04:59.480
Yes, so am I.

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:00.810
Let's sit here.

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:01.240
Okay!

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:26.870
You're hurt...

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:27.800
Stay away!

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.890
She came this way!

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:34.320
Damned monster! Where are you?!

00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:37.440
Come inside!

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:40.350
Hurry!

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:52.880
Don't just stand there, have a seat.

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:55.870
Here. It'll help with the scratches.

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:58.440
If you're scared of me, put it on yourself.

00:05:58.700 --> 00:05:59.740
I'm not!

00:06:01.700 --> 00:06:04.130
It's me I'm scared of.

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:51.490
<i>I have to find out</i>

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:54.530
<i>what I am.</i>

00:07:57.430 --> 00:07:58.550
Is that...

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:49.040
Is that a keyhole?

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:06.580
Father's handwriting...

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:13.320
Get out here, monster!

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:17.580
We know you're in there!

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:22.570
Give us the monster, Elaine!

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:25.630
We know you're hiding her in there!

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:28.070
You want something terrible 
to happen to Etty?

00:09:28.430 --> 00:09:30.080
There's no monster here!

00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:32.750
That girl is not a monster!

00:09:33.850 --> 00:09:35.270
Elaine.

00:09:36.710 --> 00:09:38.340
Listen to me.

00:09:38.730 --> 00:09:43.330
That girl is a messenger of the devil, 
and she will bring calamity to this village.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:44.840
Just look at the evidence.

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:48.600
Our village remains stricken by drought,
 and everyone is starving.

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:51.310
We're even experiencing an epidemic.

00:09:51.930 --> 00:09:53.120
I know.

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:55.870
Everyone wants to cling to hope.

00:09:56.180 --> 00:09:58.260
Everyone wants someone to blame.

00:09:59.090 --> 00:09:59.860
But...

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:02.360
How can you force that on her?

00:10:02.970 --> 00:10:04.060
Elaine...

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:09.160
Take her.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:14.000
Etty!

00:10:21.650 --> 00:10:22.780
What happened?!

00:10:23.050 --> 00:10:24.470
She really is a monster!

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:26.250
It's all her fault!

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:33.840
I'm sorry. Because of me, even you've been...

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:35.010
It's all right.

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:39.250
I'm worried about Etty, 
but they're not all bad people.

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:41.600
I'm sure they'll look after her—

00:10:42.560 --> 00:10:45.050
Elaine? Are you okay?

00:10:46.150 --> 00:10:47.630
It's nothing.

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:52.550
Is it... because of my poison?

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:53.750
No—

00:10:56.430 --> 00:10:58.540
Let us out! Elaine is...

00:10:58.810 --> 00:11:01.020
Let us out! Let us out!

00:11:06.320 --> 00:11:07.320
Elaine...

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:09.500
I promise I'll save you!

00:11:37.700 --> 00:11:38.860
Monster...

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:42.980
I wish...

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:45.910
you had died instead of Mom!

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:52.590
This is right.

00:11:53.070 --> 00:11:55.350
Distinguishing God and 
the devil can be difficult.

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:58.350
So long as there are those 
who believe in Him,

00:11:58.350 --> 00:12:00.330
the people will be saved.

00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:05.430
Filthy monster!

00:12:05.730 --> 00:12:08.350
Sacrificing Elaine wasn't enough,

00:12:08.350 --> 00:12:10.290
so you've come back yet again?

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:12.490
No... I...

00:12:13.660 --> 00:12:14.620
Etty...

00:12:16.520 --> 00:12:21.510
Calamity struck our village 
again because of this girl!

00:12:21.690 --> 00:12:26.840
If we defeat her, we can bring 
God's blessings back to us!

00:12:29.270 --> 00:12:30.400
<i>Father...</i>

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:33.170
<i>I'm sorry I didn't obey your orders.</i>

00:12:34.490 --> 00:12:35.910
<i>But I...</i>

00:12:36.510 --> 00:12:38.690
<i>wanted to stay with Elaine and Etty...</i>

00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:41.750
<i>You can do no such thing.</i>

00:12:41.750 --> 00:12:43.390
<i>Because you are...</i>

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:50.490
<i>a monster.</i>

00:12:51.150 --> 00:12:54.740
Now, capture the monster and punish her!

00:12:54.990 --> 00:12:57.240
In accordance with God's will!

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:06.760
Sheesh... I can't keep listening to this.

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:14.100
Ugly people like you aren't deserving 
of this beautiful jewel.

00:13:14.530 --> 00:13:16.770
This lovely young lady drowning in tears

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:21.650
now belongs to the 
gentleman thief, Arsène Lupin!

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:23.050
Lupin...

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:26.770
Sorry it took me so long.

00:13:26.770 --> 00:13:28.470
Wh-Who are you?

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:30.970
If you defend that monster, 
calamity will—

00:13:30.970 --> 00:13:32.470
Shut up, you worthless priest!

00:13:33.430 --> 00:13:37.340
Are you sure you haven't just been 
blaming curses and monsters

00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:40.630
for the disasters ravaging your village

00:13:41.180 --> 00:13:44.840
instead of the fact that you people 
refuse to think for yourselves?!

00:13:45.110 --> 00:13:48.800
And you force all of that upon

00:13:49.280 --> 00:13:51.310
this lone, trembling girl?!

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:54.960
Open your eyes! Use your heads!

00:13:55.380 --> 00:13:58.310
If you can't do that, 
you people are done for!

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:02.600
I've given you my warning. 
The rest is up to you.

00:14:03.630 --> 00:14:08.310
What are you doing? Quickly, go 
after that monster, and that man!

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:11.620
Do not be led astray by his words!

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:14.180
Do you want these disasters to continue?!

00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:25.050
Are you okay?

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:26.870
You're not hurt, are you?

00:14:28.690 --> 00:14:31.040
You saved me, so I'm all right.

00:14:32.170 --> 00:14:33.970
The others are worried.

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:37.000
Impey, Saint, Fran, and even Van...

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:38.880
And Drac, too.

00:14:39.530 --> 00:14:42.000
You mustn't involve yourselves 
with me anymore.

00:14:42.910 --> 00:14:45.060
I truly am a monster.

00:14:45.380 --> 00:14:49.370
I killed Elaine, and she trusted me.

00:14:50.020 --> 00:14:53.980
Etty was right. I should have died instead.

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:58.260
It can't be right for me to be
 the only one who's happy.

00:14:59.300 --> 00:15:02.870
So... I need to return this.

00:15:05.820 --> 00:15:08.840
I never told you my story, did I?

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:13.960
The reason why I want to stop 
Isaac's plan, whatever it takes.

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:17.900
It's because of what my teacher said.

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:19.670
Your teacher?

00:15:21.160 --> 00:15:21.920
Yeah.

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:26.340
To steal family and means of 
livelihood from the wicked

00:15:26.340 --> 00:15:28.310
and give them to those in need.

00:15:28.750 --> 00:15:31.480
That's the justice he taught me.

00:15:32.440 --> 00:15:33.310
But...

00:15:35.140 --> 00:15:38.560
I sensed that something was eating 
away at my teacher's heart.

00:15:42.410 --> 00:15:47.010
I became a chivalrous thief 
to atone for my sin.

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:53.620
See your own destiny, justice, and ideals 
through, even if it means your death.

00:15:54.560 --> 00:15:56.540
It's what I couldn't do.

00:15:58.740 --> 00:16:04.430
I didn't know at the time 
what he meant by his "sin."

00:16:06.890 --> 00:16:11.640
But whatever it was,
 it eventually drove him to madness.

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:16.950
So I decided to set things right.

00:16:21.360 --> 00:16:23.160
Did you rat us out to the cops?!

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:24.420
N-No!

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:25.930
Then who betrayed us?!

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:39.580
To think there's someone who 
would cry for even me...

00:16:41.950 --> 00:16:43.430
After he died,

00:16:44.070 --> 00:16:46.380
I learned what his sin was.

00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:48.920
He carried deep regret

00:16:50.470 --> 00:16:55.450
for knowing about Isaac's terrorist plot, 
but running away and doing nothing.

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:59.000
My father's... terrorist plot?

00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:01.820
That's why I came to London.

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:04.330
You know the rest.

00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:06.960
I won't let myself drown in sentimentality.

00:17:07.510 --> 00:17:10.550
But still, that man who
 I regarded as a father

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:16.100
wasn't the kind of man to die in
 a place like that after a stupid falling-out.

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:19.590
I still believe that.

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:23.600
So I also have a past I can't erase.

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:25.480
One I don't want anyone to know about.

00:17:26.740 --> 00:17:29.670
Well? Do you hate me now?

00:17:32.950 --> 00:17:36.610
And I swear I won't ever 
leave you on your own.

00:17:37.130 --> 00:17:38.660
The same goes for the others.

00:17:39.220 --> 00:17:43.070
No matter what you are, 
no matter what's in your past...

00:17:43.070 --> 00:17:44.990
None of that matters to us.

00:17:46.890 --> 00:17:49.680
But as far as I'm concerned, you're...

00:17:49.680 --> 00:17:52.880
Essential. You need my Horologium.

00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:54.970
No.

00:17:55.390 --> 00:18:01.910
At first, your Horologium and your connection
 to Isaac were my reasons for stealing you.

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:03.390
But...

00:18:04.130 --> 00:18:06.890
That night, when I ran after you,

00:18:07.250 --> 00:18:09.630
it was because I couldn't 
bear to leave you alone.

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:12.190
I wanted to protect you.

00:18:15.500 --> 00:18:17.350
When I see you smile,

00:18:17.630 --> 00:18:21.050
I truly feel that what I did was right.

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:23.230
You're no monster.

00:18:23.810 --> 00:18:25.290
To me, you're...

00:18:26.180 --> 00:18:27.800
just a normal girl.

00:18:32.860 --> 00:18:35.270
Let's head back to the others.

00:18:36.660 --> 00:18:38.550
Let's go home, Cardia.

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:56.510
You can't go this way. 
The villagers are lying in wait.

00:18:57.410 --> 00:18:59.880
Etty... Why...

00:19:01.560 --> 00:19:03.900
I can't forgive you for letting my mom die.

00:19:04.230 --> 00:19:07.400
But... I don't think you're a monster.

00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:11.220
Because I know that's what 
my mom believed, too.

00:19:14.320 --> 00:19:16.710
You're not a monster.

00:19:19.410 --> 00:19:22.640
<i>Something that had long 
been frozen in my heart</i>

00:19:23.060 --> 00:19:26.210
<i>seemed to thaw just a little bit then.</i>

00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:30.860
<i>There are many things I've destroyed</i>

00:19:31.750 --> 00:19:33.590
<i>for which I can never be forgiven.</i>

00:19:34.350 --> 00:19:36.250
<i>I still believe that.</i>

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:39.590
<i>But... even so...</i>

00:21:22.150 --> 00:21:24.040
I found it in my room.

00:21:24.820 --> 00:21:25.870
You're sure?

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:34.630
It looks like some kind 
of mathematical formula.

00:21:35.070 --> 00:21:36.970
This stuff is Fran's department.

00:21:39.620 --> 00:21:41.880
This one's just a regular letter.

00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:43.450
I'll read it, okay?

00:21:44.360 --> 00:21:47.320
"Cardia, my beloved daughter.

00:21:47.760 --> 00:21:50.840
If you should ever get lost,

00:21:50.840 --> 00:21:52.490
go to London—

00:21:52.970 --> 00:21:57.780
to St. Paul's Cathedral, where 
prayers are offered up to God.

00:21:58.180 --> 00:22:02.720
I'll be there, beginning preparations 
for my rebellion against God.

00:22:04.270 --> 00:22:09.180
The answers to all the doubts 
and insecurities you have,

00:22:09.650 --> 00:22:12.100
and your eternal peace,

00:22:12.720 --> 00:22:15.330
wait for you underground, 
beneath the cathedral.

00:22:17.110 --> 00:22:20.060
Come and walk toward a new future with me.

00:22:20.500 --> 00:22:23.030
All is for the sake of this plan...

00:22:24.070 --> 00:22:25.670
...Code: Realize."

00:22:26.680 --> 00:22:29.860
I know that term.

00:22:30.770 --> 00:22:33.950
It's very important to me.

00:22:35.430 --> 00:22:36.810
What a coincidence.

00:22:42.640 --> 00:22:44.440
I know it well, too.

00:22:45.340 --> 00:22:49.360
It's the code name of 
Isaac's terrorist plot.

00:22:50.050 --> 00:22:52.380
And their base is...

00:22:52.890 --> 00:22:54.890
St. Paul's Cathedral!

00:22:55.120 --> 00:22:56.850
My father is there, too?

00:23:07.100 --> 00:23:08.190
London is...

00:23:23.370 --> 00:23:28.260
Now, let us commence the 
creation of our new world.

00:23:28.530 --> 00:23:31.110
Watch me, Father...
